 # Feature: Users, invitations & job positions
 
-## Purpose
-Owner adds employees and assigns a **job position**. Only the company **Owner** can invite or change positions.
+## Who can invite
+| Actor | Can invite | Can assign `ai_admin` | Can change Owner |
+|-------|------------|----------------------|------------------|
+| Owner | Yes | Yes | No |
+| AI Administrator (`ai_admin`) | Yes (operational roles) | No | No |
+| Administration | Yes (operational roles) | No | No |
+| Other roles | No | No | No |
 
-## Frontend
-- Nav: **Users & positions**
-- Invite: email + job position → **Send invitation**
-- Employee list: change position → **Save position**
-- **Make AI administrator** shortcut
-- Debug token when DEBUG=true → login gate **Accept invitation**
-
-## Hierarchy
-Owner → AI Administrator → Manager/Supervisor → operational roles (reservation, contract, accounting, administration, member)
+## Navigation
+Menus without the required permission are **hidden** (not merely disabled).
+- `users` requires `team.manage` (owner, ai_admin, administration)
+- Operational roles see Chat / Tasks / Knowledge as allowed by their matrix
 
 ## Backend
-- `GET /companies/{id}/job-roles`
-- `POST /companies/{id}/invitations` `{ email, role_name }`
-- `PUT /companies/{id}/users/{id}/role` `{ role_name }`
-- `POST /auth/accept-invitation`
+- `POST /invitations` — owner or `team.manage`
+- `PUT /users/{id}/role` — owner or `team.manage` (ai_admin assign = owner only)
+- `PUT /administrators/{id}` — owner only
diff --git a/tests/test_admin_invite_job64.py b/tests/test_admin_invite_job64.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..68a445a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/test_admin_invite_job64.py
@@ -0,0 +1,66 @@
+"""Job 64 — AI admin / administration can invite; nav gated by permission."""
+
+from fastapi.testclient import TestClient
+
+from app.main import app
+
+client = TestClient(app)
+
+
+def _bootstrap():
+    res = client.post("/api/v1/demo/bootstrap")
+    assert res.status_code == 200, res.text
+    return res.json()
+
+
+def _login(email: str):
+    tok = client.post("/api/v1/auth/login", json={"email": email, "password": "demo12345"})
+    assert tok.status_code == 200, tok.text
+    body = tok.json()
+    return {
+        "Authorization": f"Bearer {body['access_token']}",
+        "X-User-ID": body["user_id"],
+    }
+
+
+def test_ai_admin_can_invite_reservation():
+    demo = _bootstrap()
+    admin = next(u for u in demo["users"] if u["role"] == "ai_admin")
+    headers = _login(admin["email"])
+    res = client.post(
+        f"/api/v1/companies/{demo['company_id']}/invitations",
+        headers=headers,
+        json={"email": "newres@example.test", "role_name": "reservation"},
+    )
+    assert res.status_code == 201, res.text
+    assert res.json().get("role_name") == "reservation"
+
+
+def test_ai_admin_cannot_invite_ai_admin():
+    demo = _bootstrap()
+    admin = next(u for u in demo["users"] if u["role"] == "ai_admin")
+    headers = _login(admin["email"])
+    res = client.post(
+        f"/api/v1/companies/{demo['company_id']}/invitations",
+        headers=headers,
+        json={"email": "otheradmin@example.test", "role_name": "ai_admin"},
+    )
+    assert res.status_code in (400, 403), res.text
+
+
+def test_reservation_cannot_invite():
+    demo = _bootstrap()
+    res_user = next(u for u in demo["users"] if u["role"] == "reservation")
+    headers = _login(res_user["email"])
+    res = client.post(
+        f"/api/v1/companies/{demo['company_id']}/invitations",
+        headers=headers,
+        json={"email": "x@example.test", "role_name": "member"},
+    )
+    assert res.status_code == 403, res.text
+
+
+def test_users_nav_requires_team_manage():
+    from pathlib import Path
+    js = Path("app/static/workspace/app.js").read_text(encoding="utf-8")
+    assert 'users: ["team.manage"]' in js or "users: ['team.manage']" in js
